---
import { RiAlertLine } from "@remixicon/react"

import Section from "@/components/brand/Section.astro"
import { OFFSET_PARTNER_URL } from "@/lib/links"

// PRODUCT.md: anything standing in for evidence that does not exist yet ships
// clearly labelled. The offset partner has not been named, so the line that
// would name them carries a caution tag saying exactly that rather than a
// plausible-looking logo.
---

<Section id="carbon" ground="field" width="wide" class="pt-14 pb-12 md:pt-24 md:pb-16">
  <p class="t-label mute">Carbon</p>
  <h2 class="t-h2">
    The power it burns is offset, and it is already paid for.
  </h2>
  <p class="t-lead">
    An AI answer costs real electricity, a great deal more than almost anything
    else your computer does in a day. The carbon that usage produces is offset,
    and the cost of doing that sits inside the prices above.
  </p>
  <p class="t-body mute">
    One person's share of this is small. So is one person's recycling. It counts
    for the same reason.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-2 border-t border-(--g-rule-firm) pt-4">
    <span class="tag w-fit text-caution">
      <RiAlertLine size={12} aria-hidden="true" />
      Placeholder · partner not named
    </span>
    <p class="t-small mute">
      The organization retiring the offsets is not named on this page yet. When
      it is, it will be linked{" "}
      <a
        class="text-(--signal-here) underline decoration-1 underline-offset-4"
        href={OFFSET_PARTNER_URL}>here</a
      >, so the claim can be read rather than trusted.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>
